// Touch range in D&D (can be cast on a willing ally), narrowed to self-only
// exactly like mage_armor.ron's/nondetection.ron's own precedent: no
// touch-a-willing-ally targeting mechanism exists for a `SelfBuff`-shaped
// spell, and the sheet's own notes explicitly call for the `SelfBuff` arm
// here. "Resistance to one chosen energy type" has no per-damage-kind
// resistance primitive to pick a specific type with, so it becomes the same
// flat, kind-agnostic `ProtectingWard` reduction this school's other energy/
// AC-style wards already use.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: ProtectingWard, data: BuffData(strength: 0.25, duration: Some(60.0))),
    ],
    energy_cost: 35.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
